.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt NATIVE-LLM-BENCH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm native-llm-bench
.Nd benchmark a native FreeBSD Vulkan GPU selected by PCI address
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -gpu Ar nvidia | radeon
.Op Fl -build Ar dir
.Op Fl -build-tag Ar tag
.Op Fl -models Ar dir
.Op Fl -out Ar rundir
.Op Fl -threads Ar n
.Op Fl -device Ar bus
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -jsonl
.Op Fl -hw-preflight Ar path
.Op Fl -icd-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -medians Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility runs the native llama.cpp Vulkan benchmark on one AMD Radeon or NVIDIA
GPU.
It selects the GPU by its PCI address, proves that the Vulkan and benchmark
paths are native
.Fx ,
checks resources before each model, and writes records for the benchmark
history.
It never falls back to a Vulkan device index or starts a Linuxulator path for
NVIDIA.
Native NVIDIA operation requires Mesa NVK on libnvrm; until that path can
create a device, an NVIDIA invocation is refused with a reference to Track
2379.
.Pp
The utility performs these stages in order and records each stage in its JSON
output:
.Bl -enum
.It
It runs
.Ic hw-preflight
with vendor 0x10de for NVIDIA or 0x1002 for Radeon and a generated device-node
map.
The Radeon map comes from
.Ic sysctl Ns 's
hw.dri busids; the NVIDIA map comes from dev.nvidia units, their parents, and
.Ic pciconf .
Exactly one verified device is required.
Several eligible devices require
.Fl -device ;
no eligible device produces status
.Dq none .
.It
It selects the unique ICD manifest whose library basename is
.Pa libvulkan_radeon.so
for Radeon.
For NVIDIA, it obtains the architecture with
.Ic uname Fl p
and selects only
.Pa nvk_nvrm_icd.<arch>.json
when that manifest's library basename is
.Pa libvulkan_nvk_nvrm.so .
For example, the aarch64 manifest is
.Pa nvk_nvrm_icd.aarch64.json .
An NVIDIA ICD in the search directory or inherited environment that names
.Pa libvulkan_nouveau.so
is refused: nouveau is not a supported path; the NVK-on-libnvrm Mesa is
required.
For either GPU, an inherited
.Ev VK_DRIVER_FILES
is accepted only when its sole entry is identical to the selected manifest.
Every other Vulkan loader, layer or dynamic-loader override is refused and
removed from the child environment.
A bare ICD library name is refused; a relative path containing a slash is
resolved beside its manifest.
It refuses manifests or libraries below a linuxroot or
.Pa /compat/linux
path, and libraries that
.Ic file Fl b
does not identify as
.Fx
from its description alone.
The selected manifest is the sole value of
.Ev VK_DRIVER_FILES
for subsequent child processes.
.It
It parses full
.Ic vulkaninfo
output and selects the GPU block whose decimal PCI domain, bus, device and
function equal the preflight address.
The required driver name is
.Dq radv
for Radeon or
.Dq NVK (CloudBSD, libnvrm)
for NVIDIA.
The Vulkan index is the block's position among non-CPU devices and is confirmed
by name with
.Ic llama-bench Fl -list-devices .
When non-CPU device names are duplicated, the complete contiguous llama-bench
name order must match vulkaninfo; otherwise selection is refused.
.It
It requires
.Ic file Fl b
to identify the llama-bench executable as a
.Fx
binary from its description alone.
NVIDIA is refused if
.Ic kldstat
and
.Ic kldstat Fl v
show linux.ko, linux64.ko, linux_common.ko, linux64elf, linuxelf or
linux_common.
For Radeon, any such modules are recorded without refusing the run.
.It
It benchmarks Llama 3.2 3B Instruct Q4_K_M with flash attention enabled, then
Llama 2 7B Q4_0 with flash attention disabled and enabled.
Each invocation uses
.Fl ngl Ar 99 ,
.Fl r Ar 3 ,
.Fl p Ar 512
and
.Fl n Ar 128 .
Before starting a model, it records host free plus inactive memory, load
average, free GPU memory, and processes holding the GPU node.
It requires model size plus 2 GiB of host memory and model size plus 1 GiB of
GPU memory.
The first failed resource check or benchmark records a failed run for that
model and records later models with the reason
.Dq skipped: an earlier run failed .
.It
It writes the raw llama-bench JSON and standard-error files, a
.Pa meta.json
run description, and a
.Pa summary.json
containing all completed rows.
The build description uses the first non-empty line that
.Ic llama-bench Fl -version
writes to standard output or standard error, followed by the build_commit value
from the benchmark JSON rows and the native build directory.
A metadata or recording failure after the benchmarks leaves the raw files in
place and still writes
.Pa summary.json
with status
.Dq error
and every completed row.
Llama 2 7B Q4_0 rows include the matching published median, its sources, and
the percentage difference rounded to one decimal.
.It
It writes one JSON document to standard output and a human-readable table to
standard error.
With
.Fl -jsonl ,
it writes one line per stage and row, followed by one summary line.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--hw-preflight path"
.It Fl -gpu Ar nvidia | radeon
Select the GPU vendor.
This option is required.
.It Fl -build Ar dir
Read llama-bench from
.Pa dir/bin/llama-bench .
The default is
.Pa $GB10_WORK/llm/b12627/build-vulkan .
.It Fl -build-tag Ar tag
Prefix the build description in
.Pa meta.json
with
.Ar tag .
For example,
.Ar b12627
records the source tag even when a shallow clone reports build number 1.
.It Fl -models Ar dir
Read the two GGUF models from
.Ar dir .
The default is
.Pa ~/work/models .
.It Fl -out Ar rundir
Write raw results and run metadata below
.Ar rundir .
The directory must be new or empty; a nonempty directory is refused with exit
2 before any file is changed.
The default is
.Pa $GB10_WORK/llm/history/runs/ Ns Ar UTC-stamp Ns -native- Ns Ar gpu Ns - Ns Ar nvk|radv ,
where the UTC stamp has the form YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.
.It Fl -threads Ar n
Pass
.Ar n
to llama-bench's
.Fl t
option.
The default is 8.
.It Fl -device Ar bus
Pass a PCI bus selector such as
.Ar pci13:1:0:0
to hw-preflight.
This is required when more than one device of the requested vendor is
eligible.
.It Fl -dry-run
Perform preflight, ICD, device and native-process checks, print the two planned
benchmark commands, and do not benchmark either model.
.It Fl -jsonl
Emit JSON Lines instead of one indented JSON document.
.It Fl -hw-preflight Ar path
Run the hardware preflight helper at
.Ar path .
The default is
.Pa ~/git/skills/skills/hardware-preflight-and-verify/scripts/hw-preflight .
.It Fl -icd-dir Ar dir
Search
.Ar dir
for Vulkan ICD JSON manifests.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/share/vulkan/icd.d .
.It Fl -medians Ar file
Read published comparisons from
.Ar file .
The default is
.Pa ../docs/published-medians.json
relative to the utility.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "NLB_HW_PREFLIGHT"
.It Ev GB10_WORK
Base directory for the default build and output paths.
The default is
.Pa ~/work/gb10 .
.It Ev VK_DRIVER_FILES
An inherited value is accepted only when its sole entry is identical to the
selected native ICD manifest.
For NVIDIA, an entry naming
.Pa libvulkan_nouveau.so
is refused.
The utility sets
.Ev VK_DRIVER_FILES
to the selected manifest for every child process after ICD selection.
.It Ev VK_ADD_DRIVER_FILES , Ev VK_ICD_FILENAMES , Ev VK_LOADER_DRIVERS_SELECT , Ev VK_LOADER_DRIVERS_DISABLE
These driver overrides are refused when set, including when empty.
.It Ev VK_LOADER_LAYERS_ENABLE , Ev VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS , Ev VK_LAYER_PATH , Ev VK_ADD_LAYER_PATH
These layer overrides are refused when set, including when empty.
.It Ev LD_PRELOAD , Ev LD_LIBRARY_PATH , Ev GGML_VK_VISIBLE_DEVICES
These dynamic-loader and device-order overrides are refused when set,
including when empty.
.It Ev NLB_TEST
Set to 1 to enable the fixture-command interface.
Test rows and metadata carry test_mode true and path_status test, never native
history provenance.
.It Ev NLB_VULKANINFO , Ev NLB_PCICONF , Ev NLB_SYSCTL , Ev NLB_KLDSTAT , Ev NLB_FSTAT , Ev NLB_FILE , Ev NLB_BECTL , Ev NLB_UNAME , Ev NLB_HW_PREFLIGHT , Ev NLB_LLAMA_BENCH
Override the corresponding external command only when
.Ev NLB_TEST
is 1.
Without it, an override produces exit 2 and names the variable.
These overrides support fixture-backed testing without a GPU or a real
llama-bench executable.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "docs/published-medians.json"
.It Pa docs/published-medians.json
Published Vulkan comparison medians and their sources.
.It Pa RUNDIR/meta.json
Run card, backend, build, software stack, active boot environment and notes.
.It Pa RUNDIR/summary.json
Completed benchmark rows, published comparisons, skipped runs and errors.
.It Pa RUNDIR/GPU-MODEL.json
Raw llama-bench JSON for one model.
.It Pa RUNDIR/GPU-MODEL.err
Standard error from the same model invocation.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n
.It 0
All requested checks and benchmarks succeeded, or a dry-run completed.
.It 1
A benchmark failed or a pre-run resource check prevented it from starting.
.It 2
Usage, input, output, metadata or an unexpected internal error.
.It 3
A non-native, ambiguous, mismatched or unavailable-driver path was refused.
.It 4
No eligible device of the requested vendor was found.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check the working native Radeon path without running either model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
native-llm-bench --gpu radeon --dry-run
.Ed
.Pp
Run both models on NVIDIA after NVK on libnvrm is installed; until then this
command refuses the path with exit 3:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
native-llm-bench --gpu nvidia
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr native-path-check 1 ,
.Xr vulkaninfo 1 ,
.Pa docs/llm.md ,
.Pa docs/published-medians.json
